      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think I still need to iterate a bit on this part after all my fiddling with it.\n\nThe handler will synchronize the message handling and make sure DISCONNECT is the next processed thing after any pending message is finished. \n\nThe unchecked boolean is common. We get a false if the message couldn\u0027t be added, which is usually because there\u0027s no looper or the handler has exited:\nhttps://source.corp.google.com/h/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/base/core/java/android/os/Handler.java;l\u003d749-751;drc\u003da780201b38d21bd9b159f83815021b050355a273\n\nIn practice, with what we have so far here, we would _probably_ start processing a disconnect, then we might abort(), which would interrupt(), if there\u0027s a pending request only. That interrupt would keep the OBEX level disconnect from working, and would instead just bring down the transport.",
      "parentUuid": "92cab139_60115a7f",
